diff --git a/docs/prewarm.md b/docs/prewarm.md
index 935c53896..581f9d998 100644
--- a/docs/prewarm.md
+++ b/docs/prewarm.md
@@ -18,8 +18,36 @@ Workers still install their own filters before running device code.
 `vmm.prepare` accepts `vcpu_ids`, consecutive IDs starting at zero (at most
 256). KVM descriptor creation happens before restore; architectural state
 initialization stays in the existing CPU restore path. Unused descriptors
-are owned by the prepared VM and dropped with it. Empty IDs retain generic prewarm only.
+are owned by the prepared VM and dropped with it. Empty IDs with no device profile retain generic prewarm only.
 
 Prepared vCPU IDs must match the actual restored boot CPU count and topology.
 A mismatch is rejected before restoring state or preparing template memory;
 unused reserved kernel vCPUs are never silently attached to a different VM.
+
+## Profile prewarm device workers
+
+A profile can also specify `block_queues` (one count per block device),
+`net_queues` (even RX/TX queue counts, excluding the control queue), `console`,
+`rng`, `pmem` (device count), `vsock`, and `balloon`. These capacity hints
+reserve at most 256 one-shot workers. Block devices use one worker per queue;
+network devices use one per queue pair plus one control worker. Each other
+listed device uses one worker. `workers` in the response is the reserved count.
+
+Workers wait without device or guest state. First activation transfers the
+ordinary seccomp and panic/error wrapper to a matching worker. No device
+trait extension is needed: resources flow through the transport's existing
+activation context to its worker collection. Exhaustion or a kind/seccomp
+mismatch uses ordinary allocation. Hotplug, reset and subsequent activation
+do not reuse the initial reserve. Unused workers are joined on delete or a
+failed preparation; consumed handles keep the normal device cleanup rules.
+
+Set process cgroups, NUMA policy, nice level and other inherited placement
+before preparation, and keep those settings stable for the prepared process.
+Do not individually reconfigure parked workers. Reuse is restricted to the
+creating VMM thread with unchanged affinity, signal mask and scheduler
+policy/priority; mismatches use ordinary thread creation. The VMM seccomp
+filter adds only read-only scheduler queries for this check. Device filters
+and the activation-time filter installation are unchanged.
+
+Restores with Landlock enabled discard device reservations and use ordinary
+allocation, so workers inherit restrictions at the normal activation point.
